Like, I think it also, as much space as there is to play with those things, there's also a lot of room to be lazy.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:29.160
But if bugs just had like some, if bugs just had some basic power ups, like TNT that he could plant and it would take three seconds and then blow up or even more creatively, he could go up against the side of a wall and draw like a, you know, like this is more of a wild coyote kind of thing.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:35.740
But like, you know, draw that and then enemies actually walk into that instead of through him or just like collect a disguise.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:40.440
Like there are multiple bugs disguised and they all act the same, but it's kind of funny to see him dressed in.

00:14:41.160 --> 00:14:42.000
Yeah, sure, sure.

00:14:42.140 --> 00:14:43.760
But like, not really.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.740
You know what? More like a woman, right?

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:46.940
Like bugs does that often.

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.660
And then it's like now enemies don't know that he's bugs bunny.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.840
So they don't hurt you for a little bit.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:54.900
Like while you have that power up, these are all solid ideas.

00:14:54.900 --> 00:15:04.400
You know what I think like a simple power up that you could like evolve throughout the game would be is just when you walk off a ledge, just let you walk a little further.

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:09.500
Like, you know, like a glide ability, but having that like I'm still walking until I realize that I'm going to fall.

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:12.900
Yeah, like that's like, that's like iconic Looney Tunes.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.720
That's, that's a great, that's a great example.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.060
And I am just working off memory here.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:21.120
So I could be completely just working on childhood brain.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:30.920
But I recall Gex64, otherwise known as Gex Enter the Gecko on other platforms, had like a Looney Tunes level in it.

00:15:31.000 --> 00:15:35.920
This is the one where he like, Gex goes into different like TV channels and ones like the Titanic.

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:39.540
And then this one, that's weird that one's the Titanic, but I remember that.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:43.340
This one was like a Looney Tunes themed thing.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:50.500
And like that is a better like representation of Looney Tunes in a video game than any Looney Tunes video game I've ever played.

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:54.800
I honestly can't think of too many other Looney Tunes games that I've played.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:16:02.500
I played a great Space Jam Looney Tunes game on PC that was basically NBA Jam, but like skinned with Looney Tunes characters.

00:16:02.720 --> 00:16:11.240
That was pretty good because during the halftime show, you had to go back to Michael Jordan's house to pick up his shoes and other stuff and not get detected by the dog.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:13.200
That's a good idea.

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:14.400
It's a great idea.

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.780
Should have happened before the game though, realistically.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.580
Anyway, coming back to the game.

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:22.440
There's mini games.

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.640
Those take us out of the, you know, those are like a little sillier.

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.840
He's doing like whack-a-mole and stuff like that.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:29.500
And slots.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:31.820
Yeah, slots slash bingo.

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:36.160
What's the bonus round thing too with like all the numbers all over the place?

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:38.380
I think that's like bingo.

00:16:38.380 --> 00:16:44.400
Yeah, it's like bingo that, yeah, and I think there, it just is bingo.

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:46.520
Sorry, I shouldn't have interrupted Joe.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.160
It's a very complicated way of doing it.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.360
I think it is actually the combination of a bingo slot machine.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:59.120
You like spin numbers and whatever it lands on is like what you have on your bingo board.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:11.140
And you get extra lives from that and if you get five in a row with how unlikely that is, you get 15 extra lives, which is insane.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:21.480
Yeah, more than you need in Bugs Bunny Birthday Blow because, you know, not that it's a good or bad thing, but I don't think I lost any lives while playing this game.

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:26.000
Like ever. Also, I'm not entirely sure how the hearts work.

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:31.400
I think they like turn white and that means they get one more hit and then they disappear.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:36.240
So like they're red and then you get hit once, it turns white, then you get hit again, it disappears.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:39.500
And now you only have, now you don't have that heart until you fill it back up.

00:17:39.840 --> 00:17:44.500
It just, it looks like, yeah, you would, it would be something you fill up, but then they just go away.

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:47.440
Yeah, but I mean, if you find another heart, it'll come back.

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.700
Oh, okay. Got it.

00:17:49.780 --> 00:17:50.860
So I think it is like filling up.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.960
It's just like it doesn't show the empty heart container.

00:17:53.220 --> 00:17:55.020
Like it just, it's just gone when it's empty.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:21.680
The boss fights are also kind of weird because I don't even want to call them boss fights, but they're like the only moment where you see other Looney Tunes characters from the show.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:28.920
And like, they're not particularly challenging, but also they don't seem like they're ready to be the boss fight.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:32.280
Like you could, you could just attack them really fast and be done with it.

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:36.200
It takes like two or three hits to the mallet on some of these guys.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.940
But they don't do anything like that.

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:42.060
Yeah. That's all that challenging or different.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:52.260
I think this is just a side effect of the, these issues with like game feel that we were talking about earlier where like, you, I can see where, where they're going.

00:18:52.260 --> 00:18:55.080
Like what they're trying to do with these boss fights.

00:18:55.240 --> 00:19:00.220
Like Daffy is always somebody that you got to, uh, just outrun.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:01.600
Not interact with at all.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:05.200
Not interact with. Yeah. Classic Bugs Bunny Daffy Duck interaction.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:12.180
Tweety. You got kind of got to lure him out and take a hit because you can't hit him in the bush.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:19.820
Um, uh, the Elmer shoots at you and he's actually like, you know, there's actually projectiles.

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:33.100
You got to dodge. And, um, I think, and I forgot the other ones, but they all kind of have a thing, but they're, it's all, it all means nothing because all you do is you go and you hit them and then they go away.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:44.620
I think you hit them three times or so and there's no mechanical trick to learn because it's not hard enough to need to know patterns or anything.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:49.200
And there's no feedback when you're hitting them until suddenly they just drop right.

00:19:49.480 --> 00:19:54.700
Yeah. The sprite just turns upside down while it's still in the same position and then falls down through the screen.

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.740
Like, ah, ah, what the hell is that?

00:19:57.940 --> 00:20:00.740
I don't want to see Pepe Le Pew upside down.

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:01.900
Like he's a dead goldfish.

00:20:01.900 --> 00:20:03.560
Oh yeah. He farted. That was his thing.

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:05.720
I mean, that is kind of his thing in the show.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:11.360
So that's actually one of the few moments in this game where it's working to its benefit.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.520
You know, it's a moment where I realized that the game, uh, might not be good.

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:17.420
What's that? The ending.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:20.540
Oh, and they were all just like, we were just joshing.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:27.520
Yeah, they were just joshing, but also it's like, okay, so it says finally Bugs Bunny arrives at his party and it's got a shot, you know, like that's text.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.680
That's a huge text box, way too much text box screen for the amount of text on it.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:36.580
But then there's another box with an image of Bugs opening up a door very strangely.

00:20:36.580 --> 00:20:43.380
Like he has like one foot in the air and two hands on the doors as if like it takes that kind of strength to get into this house.

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:48.060
But he's, he's like, he's in mid motion of it, right?

00:20:48.340 --> 00:20:53.360
Then it says on another text box after you hit the A button, he enters dot dot dot.

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:59.600
Couldn't we just get like one more like image of him entering instead of the text box?

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:06.000
Like it was easier for them to just put in he enters a stage direction than draw us one more scene.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:09.620
Like that's the kind of level of detail we're talking about here in the game.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:18.420
I thought that the he enters was to be like, cause the only way to show him entering is to show, this doesn't, this is already, as I'm saying it, falling apart my theory here.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:24.100
But if they show him entering, it's like he enters, that's the suspenseful moment.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:28.440
And then it's like, surprise, there's his friends are all there, but the next screen doesn't show his friends anyway.

00:21:28.460 --> 00:21:30.200
So it doesn't really matter.

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:35.140
Right, and I'm not saying the next screen should say he enters, he should just be in the next room and it says.

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:36.480
He should just have entered? Yeah.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:37.820
Yeah, he should just have entered.

00:21:38.100 --> 00:21:39.340
Does he just teleport there?

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:42.760
He just is, the door, we can only assume.

00:21:42.960 --> 00:21:44.120
I can't, no, no, no.

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:49.300
It turned into a comic book now, they don't even want to animate it, they're literally just giving us like four stills.

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:56.540
I don't even think they need to animate it, but like he is, the more I'm, the more I'm looking at it, the more I'm seeing your, I was like, why are you hung up on this?

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:58.560
But now I'm like indignant that this has happened.

00:21:58.560 --> 00:22:01.100
Because he's opening the door, he's walking through the door.

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:02.500
Yes. We see him entering.

00:22:02.680 --> 00:22:04.460
It's like they're questioning our intelligence.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:07.820
Who's to say that he isn't just leaning on a door?

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:09.300
That's a good point.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:14.100
It is a weird way to open a door or to lean, so you never know.

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:22.500
And then you see bugs actually, like you guys said, all the boss fights with Taz and Sylvester and...

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:24.460
Elmer is shooting a gun at you, by the way.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:25.880
Yeah, yeah, Tweety Bird.

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:31.080
Edward, they're all like at the party now and you guys take a picture in front of the Bugs Bunny sign.

00:22:31.360 --> 00:22:34.040
It doesn't say the there, it just says Bugs Bunny.

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:35.580
But you take a picture in front of that sign.

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:37.680
Obviously, Daffy must be there.

00:22:37.740 --> 00:22:38.900
He's the one who took the picture.

00:22:40.380 --> 00:22:41.560
But like... Foghorn?

00:22:41.700 --> 00:22:42.560
Leghorn wasn't...

00:22:42.560 --> 00:22:44.120
Yeah, who else is there?

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:47.040
That's what I'm saying. Like, who was invited to this party?

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:50.420
It seems like only the people who thought they weren't invited wound up at the party.

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:58.120
So, yeah, I think that just brings into question, like, are we being lied to as the audience?

00:22:58.720 --> 00:23:01.440
And if so, who's lying to us?

00:23:02.240 --> 00:23:11.800
Because it sounds like, oh, they were just like trying to, you know, make sure they had enough time to get ready while Bugs Bunny was on their way to the party.

00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:14.420
Because they obviously knew they were all invited.

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:20.120
So, what pretext did they have otherwise to tell us the player?

00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:21.340
I don't know.

00:23:21.720 --> 00:23:22.940
Maybe. Were they invited?

00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.100
So, they just showed up?

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:26.600
Yeah, they just showed up.

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:30.840
The whole premise... I forgot that the whole premise at the beginning was that they're mad that they weren't invited.

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:33.100
And then it's like, surprise, we weren't mad, actually.

00:23:33.160 --> 00:23:34.560
But it's like, well, what are you doing at my party?

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:36.140
And where's everybody else?

00:23:36.260 --> 00:23:39.980
I think we as the player are being lied to by the narrator.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:41.960
By, no, by, yeah, Chuck Jones.

00:23:42.140 --> 00:23:43.320
Unreliable narrator. The director.

00:23:45.860 --> 00:23:49.480
Chuck Jones did not work on this game, but I think that's funny either way.

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:52.120
Happy birthday, Bugs Bunny, and congratulations.

00:23:54.100 --> 00:23:55.700
Congratulations on a birthday, right?

00:23:56.240 --> 00:23:58.880
Well, you know, getting the 50s, nothing to sneeze at.

00:23:59.060 --> 00:23:59.980
You know, that was all you.

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:04.980
I'm surprised it didn't say, like, happy birthday, Bugs Bunny, and congratulations, Warner Brothers.

00:24:05.200 --> 00:24:07.640
You know, like, one more shot to get WB in there.

00:24:09.980 --> 00:24:11.140
Thank you, Warner Brothers.

00:24:11.780 --> 00:24:20.860
While we're on the subject, though, of, you know, like, actual Looney Tunes stuff and the director, Chuck Jones, and we could mention other people, too.

00:24:21.000 --> 00:24:33.180
But, like, one of the most famous composers for Looney Tunes, Carl Stalling, who made most of the, you know, not music that you could instantly recognize, but if you heard it, you'd be like, yeah, that must have been on Looney Tunes.

00:24:33.540 --> 00:24:35.540
That is lacking in this game as well.

00:24:35.840 --> 00:24:37.880
And, again, it's 8-bit, like, what can they do?

00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:44.520
But, like, they could have leaned into some of his merry melodies, for lack of a better word.

00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:49.760
Yeah. And really had fun with that, because that's another iconic part of Looney Tunes.

00:24:49.900 --> 00:24:51.860
It's in the name. They're silly songs.

00:24:52.080 --> 00:24:54.120
But silly songs was actually Disney, so.

00:24:54.600 --> 00:25:03.520
I do think that on an 8-bit console, like, one of the few things that just you can do is, like, da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da-da.

00:25:03.660 --> 00:25:08.020
Like, it's just, like, not, like, that's made for 8-bit, like, NES music.

00:25:08.440 --> 00:25:10.580
Agreed. Maybe there's some licensing problem.

00:25:10.920 --> 00:25:13.900
But even then, you could have found something that sounded like it, you know?

00:25:14.040 --> 00:25:16.460
Or just hired somebody to make something sound like it.

00:25:16.460 --> 00:25:19.800
I don't know. I thought of another highlight moment in the game.

00:25:19.960 --> 00:25:29.440
Another great moment for Looney Tunes comedy, and that is those little seesaws that you go on, and you have to hit the mallet to go high in the air.

00:25:29.980 --> 00:25:33.600
That's the kind of shit we needed, like, times 100 in this game.

00:25:33.700 --> 00:25:35.540
Yeah, I like that stuff. That's what Joe was getting at, yeah.

00:25:35.540 --> 00:25:39.660
Yeah, taking credit for my opinion.

00:25:40.460 --> 00:25:41.260
Classic Mike.

00:25:41.500 --> 00:25:50.400
I was only listening to the part of your other genius idea, which was when you said to run off the platform and just go get, like, another second or so before you die.

00:25:51.040 --> 00:25:57.240
But, you know, one of the more cartoony things that I noticed in this was the pause animation.

00:25:57.660 --> 00:26:04.320
It's been a long time since we've done the pause sound, but this one is more, not so much about the sound, which was just a kind of generic pause sound, but the animation.

00:26:04.320 --> 00:26:09.320
The word pause comes up on the screen and does just countless backflips.

00:26:10.220 --> 00:26:18.380
Yeah. It's probably the most advanced pause graphic in the history of this console.

00:26:18.800 --> 00:26:23.840
Yeah, and that's where all their, like, Looney Tunes creativity went, was into the pause graphic.

00:26:24.100 --> 00:26:28.680
We need to find out who made the pause animation and see what other work they did.

00:26:28.680 --> 00:26:30.740
Get them on the show. That's worth chasing.

00:26:31.060 --> 00:26:32.480
Tim Follins, I think.

00:26:34.020 --> 00:26:35.420
He should have been doing the music.

00:26:35.600 --> 00:26:37.880
He should have gotten the hell off the animation.

00:26:38.900 --> 00:26:44.100
Anybody want to try to explain the carrot boxes instead of just picking up carrots?

00:26:44.900 --> 00:26:53.880
I think that they had an idea of having the item boxes then become platforms and weren't entirely sure how to do that.

00:26:54.820 --> 00:27:07.800
Yeah. I'm not going to say that it's a great idea, but it is at least something that you can interact with in a different way than just, like, a standard platform.

00:27:07.800 --> 00:27:10.560
So maybe it was just to keep it the same shape.

00:27:10.560 --> 00:27:16.200
Yeah, but what it is is that the carrot, when the carrot is on there, it is not a platform.

00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:20.680
You have to go, you have to move through it once before it becomes a platform.

00:27:21.140 --> 00:27:25.720
So that makes it, like, I mean, yeah, I also don't know if I think this is, like, a good or a bad thing.

00:27:25.800 --> 00:27:27.740
But I was, I found this interesting.

00:27:27.760 --> 00:27:30.060
It did make me think about things more often.

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:32.640
I feel like I'd have to let it sit longer to see if I like it.

00:27:32.820 --> 00:27:35.280
I mean, I think it also depends on how the game was designed around it.

00:27:35.280 --> 00:27:45.720
But there were times where I would have to think, I'm not sure if this is by design, but I would have to think, like, okay, if I jump up through this, then I can land on it because I'll have already transformed it.

00:27:45.900 --> 00:27:48.980
But I got to make sure I'm not jumping down through it because then I'll just continue falling.

00:27:49.580 --> 00:27:52.900
In Japan, this game is known as Happy Birthday Bugs.

00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:54.320
Is that a better title?

00:27:54.780 --> 00:27:55.860
I actually don't think so.

00:27:56.260 --> 00:28:00.240
I don't either. I mean, sounds like a song you would sing to him.

00:28:01.300 --> 00:28:06.320
Yeah, the Bugs Bunny birthday blowout thing that we were joking about the the at the beginning.

00:28:06.580 --> 00:28:12.560
But, like, outside of that, that sounds like an extravagant, like, it sounds like, wow, this game is going to be a blast.

00:28:12.800 --> 00:28:16.780
Yeah, I don't think it's worthy of the blowout, like, moniker.

00:28:17.140 --> 00:28:22.380
Like, blowout is really, like, oh, and we put everything Bugs Bunny in this game.

00:28:22.480 --> 00:28:27.020
And it's like, well, I think it's just a misnomer because you don't get to see the party.

00:28:27.020 --> 00:28:28.960
And you can't really call a party.

00:28:29.200 --> 00:28:31.620
And blowout usually will refer to a party.

00:28:31.940 --> 00:28:37.680
And if we don't see the party being a blowout, who's to say it actually was, you know?

00:28:38.720 --> 00:28:41.420
We did something similar at Nickelodeon with SpongeBob.

00:28:41.580 --> 00:28:45.920
We had SpongeBob's big birthday blowout, and we also never showed his party.

00:28:48.320 --> 00:28:49.240
So it can happen.

00:28:49.260 --> 00:28:51.280
But it was all Nickelodeon logos all around.

00:28:51.520 --> 00:28:54.920
Yeah, SpongeBob and Patrick were collecting Nickelodeon logos.

00:28:54.920 --> 00:29:01.420
Yeah. Also, in Europe, it's just the Bugs Bunny blowout.

00:29:01.780 --> 00:29:03.580
They dropped the birthday part.

00:29:04.320 --> 00:29:08.380
Oh. I doubt they dropped it throughout the entirety of the game, though.

00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:10.060
So now that makes, that's worse.

00:29:11.120 --> 00:29:14.520
Maybe it's like, maybe it was trying to be like the Bugs Bunny anniversary blowout.

00:29:14.560 --> 00:29:15.680
Because that's really what this is.

00:29:15.860 --> 00:29:16.940
It's not his birthday.

00:29:17.200 --> 00:29:18.640
It's his anniversary of, like.

00:29:18.780 --> 00:29:23.960
Yeah, yeah. I guess, I guess we're, let's get in the weeds of what's canonically Bugs' birthday.

00:29:23.960 --> 00:29:26.920
Because we still have so many interesting things to talk about.

00:29:27.200 --> 00:29:28.320
Bugs Bunny, though.

00:29:28.980 --> 00:29:30.300
Just thinking about it.

00:29:30.900 --> 00:29:31.820
Bugs Bunny.

00:29:32.200 --> 00:29:34.140
First appearance. 1938.

00:29:34.780 --> 00:29:35.620
Steamboat Willie.

00:29:37.660 --> 00:29:38.960
1938, right?

00:29:39.280 --> 00:29:43.020
So this is actually like his 52nd anniversary?

00:29:43.400 --> 00:29:44.760
Like, you can't celebrate it.

00:29:44.960 --> 00:29:45.860
The game's 1990.

00:29:45.860 --> 00:29:48.640
But the game takes place in 88.

00:29:49.060 --> 00:29:50.860
The game takes place.

00:29:51.100 --> 00:29:52.520
